{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/372576-project-vauldrie-and-the-ccp-c-d","id":372576,"title":"Project Vauldrie and the CCP C&D","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-16T08:52:16-08:00","id":372576,"title":"Project Vauldrie and the CCP C&D","content":"While I'm surprised that no one in this forum has brought this up but to get everyone's attention, was anyone aware that <a href=\"http://www.projectvaulderie.com/goodnight-sweet-prince/\" target=\"_blank\">CCP shut down Project Vauldrie last year</a>? To be honest I'm quite angry at this because not only CCP canceled the MMO game, but they also had to go after fan based projects which is final straw worthy here and plus Project Vauldrie was the last hope that community had and CCP delivered the final nail in the coffin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T09:55:52-08:00","id":372664,"title":"","content":"A) CCP owns the World of Darkness and can do what they want with it.<br /> <br /> B) This is an Onyx Path forum. Onyx Path is publishing World of Darkness table top games only with CCP's permission. Onyx Path does not have any video game rights. Complaining here will do you no good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:13:19-08:00","id":372686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/372576-project-vauldrie-and-the-ccp-c-d?p=372664#post372664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) CCP owns the World of Darkness and can do what they want with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because they own and can do everything they want with it doesn't mean they deserve it. This is one of the reasons how capitalism is such a flawed system.<br /> <br /> Well even though Oynx Path doesn't have video game rights, I think I'm just trying to create some awareness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:32:30-08:00","id":372717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/372576-project-vauldrie-and-the-ccp-c-d?p=372686#post372686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because they own and can do everything they want with it doesn't mean they deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this statement even mean? They don't <i>deserve </i>to own a property? Who should decide the criteria ownership? Ownership rights aren't based on some nebulous meritocracy.<br /> <br /> I am not super happy about how CCP handled the game, and I am downright salty that I will apparently never be able to play a WoD MMO... but complaining about capitalism(?) isn't really here or there. If you wanted to talk about how jacked up the current copyright situation is, I am not sure this is the best venue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T11:36:18-08:00","id":372760,"title":"","content":"We really can't help. None of Onyx Path's current projects are computer games, and any action CCP takes on computer games is, currently, completely independent of us.<br /> <br /> If you'd like to contact CCP, the address is <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#215054445255484e4f526156494855440c564e4d470f424e4c\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"d3a2a6b6a0a7babcbda093a4bbbaa7b6fea4bcbfb5fdb0bcbe\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:42:21-08:00","id":372900,"title":"","content":"I'm also mildly surprised. CCP and white wolf have been fairly tolerant of fan projects in the past. They know that people enjoy the games (tabletop and computer both) and generally give people doing unpaid fan tweaks freedom to do what they want. Courts in multiple countries have generally ruled that uncompensated fan derivative works of products do not threaten the intellectual property rights. This is why people can draw mickey mouse for their own amusement/purposes without too much worry about Disney launching a sueball... there's no real risk.<br /> <br /> However that goes out the window when you start to profit from a derivative work. That's a direct threat that can cause the particular IP to be shifted out of the ownership of the owner and into public domain early.<br /> <br /> I find it hard to believe that the people working on Vauldrie didn't have at least someone realize the distinction between unpaid fan work and work for which someone gets paid and raised the concern before they started taking donations for the work and talking about fund raising efforts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:22:59-08:00","id":373104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/372576-project-vauldrie-and-the-ccp-c-d?p=372900#post372900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also mildly surprised. CCP and white wolf have been fairly tolerant of fan projects in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but this also isn't the first fan project that's been shut down, so it's not like this is entirely unprecedented. Years before the CCP merger, fans were making their own Revised version of the <i>Oblivion</i> LARP rules called <i>Laws of Oblivion</i>. That project was shut down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it hard to believe that the people working on Vauldrie didn't have at least someone realize the distinction between unpaid fan work and work for which someone gets paid and raised the concern before they started taking donations for the work and talking about fund raising efforts. </div> </div> </div>You may be surprised.<br /> <br /> One of the people on the Vaulderie team was Stephen Webb, who previously (Feb 2013) had a Kickstarter for <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/2144679402/requiem-of-the-night-a-modern-nights-vampire-video\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem of the Night</a>, &quot;a First Person Shooter / Role Playing Game hybrid set in the Old World of Darkness. Players can expect both single and multiplayer game modes with high-end content - and all of the traditional VTM clans.&quot; It was rightfully shut down. Then, as part of &quot;Team Ravenous,&quot; Webb started (May 2013) <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1868686619/sanguine-nights-darkest-blood\" target=\"_blank\">Sanguine Nights: Darkest Blood</a>, which like RotN, was a RPG/FPS hybrid programmed in Unity. From the looks of things, it was just RotN scrubbed of any potentially infringing material. SNDB even uses a horned eye symbol nearly identical to one used on the RotN page. SNDB failed to fund.<br /> <br /> So Project Vaulderie seemed to be Webb's third attempt to do a RPG/FPS hybrid in Unity using vampires as a base. You'd think the outcome could have been predicted in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T10:58:29-08:00","id":373618,"title":"","content":"Just one of the many reasons is I'm so anti-CCP. Again, just one of the <b>many</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T12:27:55-08:00","id":373668,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I can understand why people would be frustrated with CCP. To play devil\u2019s advocate, I\u2019m grateful. If not for its licensing agreement with Onyx Path, these discussion boards would have significantly less forums. While I can\u2019t defend CCP, I still thank them for letting Rich et al. do their thing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">There but for the grace of <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">[CCP] </span>go I\u2026</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}